Package: hd-report
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3, systemd, hd-config
Suggests: hd-dashboard
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian status reports for the dashboard
 Sends the state of the system to the hyprdebian dashboard of hd-dashboard
 every 15 minutes: the HyprDebian and Debian versions, the kernel, the state
 of Secure Boot, the load, the memory, the ZFS pools, the mdadm arrays, the
 failed units, the pending upgrades and reboots, the last snapshot of hd-up
 and the timers. The system only makes outgoing connections.
 .
 The URL of the dashboard is the key hd-report in
 /etc/hyprdebian/config.json; the token of the system is generated on the
 first installation in /etc/hyprdebian/hd-report/token. Installing the
 package enables hd-report.timer.
